The core mismatch is present, but several premises need narrowing: RGB GET now reads bytes 0–2, `#505` changed which unfilled bytes it reads at narrow widths, and one pixel operation can call the helper more than once. I also found six zero-fill sites in `memory_rw.c`, rather than three. I’m checking the MTE branch and regression assertions next.
