420-#
421-#  scored **8/8, a CLEAN SWEEP**, because every row above drives LIN_A (tlb_mode 4) and `linear' is
422-#  therefore true in all of them.  `linear' is `tlb_mode > 3' and it DOMINATES the edited lines via
423-#  the `if (!linear && (x < 0 || ...)) return;' guard, so it sits inside the DEPENDS-ON closure --
424-#  this is a floor breach, not coverage debt.
425-#
426-#  The seat that named the axis proposed conditioning on `tileptr'.  That cannot work as stated:
427-#  `tileptr &= ~0x80000000' strips the linear flag BEFORE the switch, so `tileptr' carries no
428-#  addressing-mode information by the time the arm runs.  `linear' is the variable that survives, and
429-#  building the mutant in the form the source permits is what turned a prediction into a measurement.
430-#
431-#  THE SOURCE is tiled and the DESTINATION stays LIN_A, deliberately: the RGB arm under test is the
432-#  GET, and the GET's `linear' comes from src_mode.  A tiled DESTINATION would exercise the PUT and
